{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 144, :comments ["<b>Righteousness</b> — The vav of עדותיך is like the vav of לא שלותי, and both are in place of heh, for the letters yod, heh, vav, alef interchange." "The meaning of הבינני צדק לעולם ואחיה — עולם stands in place of two [words]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 119, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra indicates that לעולם here carries the sense of two expressions (i.e., 'forever' + 'eternal'); translated hyper-literally without expanding."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:55.878008952Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}